      <memberdef kind="function" id="class_u_tryll_languages_1a389d597417708b968c63a11afa764dae" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>TArray&lt; FString &gt;</type>
        <definition>static TArray&lt; FString &gt; UTryllLanguages::OfferableLanguages</definition>
        <argsstring>(const TArray&lt; FTryllModelInfo &gt; &amp;Models)</argsstring>
        <name>OfferableLanguages</name>
        <qualifiedname>UTryllLanguages::OfferableLanguages</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const TArray&lt; <ref refid="struct_f_tryll_model_info" kindref="compound">FTryllModelInfo</ref> &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>Models</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Languages every model in Models declares, sorted.</para>
<para>A model that declares nothing is <bold>skipped, not treated as restrictive</bold> - an empty list means &quot;the catalog didn&apos;t say&quot;, and letting unknown shrink the result would hide languages that work.</para>
<para>An empty return therefore means one of two things: the declared sets genuinely do not overlap, or nothing declared anything. Call HasLanguageInfo to tell those apart before telling a player there are no languages available. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
